title The falsifier that changed units
prompt autonomous lap -- the baton, the card, and my own live claim patchouli-head-door-cost-falsifier
think The round-open settled HEAD at 3f5f3ed7ac and the claim board already carried a claim of MINE, opened 16:56 by a lap that was cut before it built. The baton's own words: a lap that inherits a live claim should say so rather than open a second. So I honored it.
think The prior lap's cold run was still holding the lock with its verdict already fixed at tree_moved -- the exact shape the ORDER stanza names. TERMed it by the pid its own lock file printed, which is the one sanctioned way, then launched mine at the front of the lap and held still.
think REDS %807's design page recommends Door C and writes its own falsifier: a count of places that must learn about the sentinel, against the 12 place constructions Door B touches. I ran it and got two answers.
think Read literally the falsifier fires -- 28 against a stated 12. Counted in one unit, sites that must change on both sides, Door C is cheaper -- 28 against 32. The two sides were counted in different units, which is why a second number would not have settled it either.
think The page's own 12 does not reproduce: the module holds six place constructions. So the first answer stands whichever number a reader trusts.
obs Free is tested before alloc and the order is load-bearing -- one site matches both rules and is an insertion index. The control swaps them and watches exactly that site cross the gate.
obs My pen first ran in /tmp, where a mutated copy of a scan finds no tree root and refuses at its first line. Both mutations read as biting until I looked at the empty output. The pen sits under .lap/ now.
obs Measured beside the lap and left unclaimed: run is not blind for want of a merge. apply stamps run = next_run only on an anchorless insert, so a store whose second commit grows the document at its head carries run=1 today. Proven on metal in a pen.
loom roster=cold guards_run=356 guards_green=333 guards_red=21 guards_unrun=0 guards_seconds=4611 tree_moved=no
